<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
<!--
  Split into three on 31 July, session 9, because the previous two values collapsed a
  judgment about evidence together with a fact about the reader.

    nobody_said     the reader read the artifact and nothing in it bears on this
                    proposition. A judgment about the evidence, and the honest majority
                    case.
    model_declined  the reader read the artifact, found the proposition discussed, and
                    could not reach a verdict. Also a judgment about the evidence.
    not_returned    the reader never reported this proposition at all. NOT a judgment
                    about anything. It is a charter-quality signal and it must never be
                    counted as an abstention: a rate that includes it measures how well a
                    charter follows its own output schema, not how often evidence was silent.

  model_missed is RETIRED and kept in the set only so rows written before the split stay
  valid. Nothing writes it. It was ambiguous between the last two values above, which is
  exactly what made the 31 July pass-one result impossible to diagnose after the fact.
  Ruled: backfill nothing, the enum starts clean, old rows keep what they were written with.

  KNOWN GAP, recorded rather than quietly worked around. AAO_Outcome__c has no value meaning
  "the reader did not report this", so a not_returned row still carries Outcome = Abstained.
  Any query counting abstentions by outcome therefore overcounts, and the correct query
  filters on this field. Adding a value to that picklist changes a CLOSED table and needs
  ratifying.
-->
    <fullName>AAO_Abstention_Reason__c</fullName>
    <description>Written by: Extraction. Read by: the abstention-rate detector, which must exclude not_returned because that value is a charter-quality signal and not a judgment about evidence. model_missed is retired and kept only so pre-split rows stay valid.</description>
    <label>Abstention Reason</label>
    <type>Picklist</type>
    <required>false</required>
    <valueSet>
        <restricted>true</restricted>
        <valueSetDefinition>
            <sorted>false</sorted>
            <value>
                <fullName>nobody_said</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>nobody_said</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>model_declined</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>model_declined</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>not_returned</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>not_returned</label>
            </value>
            <value>
                <fullName>model_missed</fullName>
                <default>false</default>
                <label>model_missed (retired)</label>
            </value>
        </valueSetDefinition>
    </valueSet>
</CustomField>
